  "difficulty": 4,
  "marks": 3,
  "estimatedSeconds": 270,
  "stem": "For $\\mathbf{a} = a_1\\mathbf{i} + a_2\\mathbf{j} + a_3\\mathbf{k}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = b_1\\mathbf{i} + b_2\\mathbf{j} + b_3\\mathbf{k}$, show that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = 0$, and state what this shows.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "markScheme": {
    "points": [
     {
      "id": "p1",
      "description": "M1 writes a × b = (a₂b₃ − a₃b₂, a₃b₁ − a₁b₃, a₁b₂ − a₂b₁).",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "A1 expands a · (a × b) and shows every term cancels to 0.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p3",
      "description": "B1 concludes a × b is perpendicular to a.",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "modelAnswer": "$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = a_1(a_2b_3 - a_3b_2) + a_2(a_3b_1 - a_1b_3) + a_3(a_1b_2 - a_2b_1)\n$$\n$$\n= a_1a_2b_3 - a_1a_3b_2 + a_2a_3b_1 - a_1a_2b_3 + a_1a_3b_2 - a_2a_3b_1 = 0\n$$\nThe scalar product is zero, so $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$ is perpendicular to $\\mathbf{a}$ (and similarly to $\\mathbf{b}$)."
  },
  "markingMode": "MANUAL",
  "explanation": "Expand and pair the six terms; each appears once with each sign.",
  "hints": [
